'''Fratelli Vineyards''' is an Indian [[winery]] based in [[Akluj]], [[Solapur]] District, [[Maharashtra]] region of India.<ref>{{Cite web |title=MSN |url=https://www.msn.com/en-in/money/topstories/fratelli-vineyards-to-debut-on-exchanges-aims-to-become-650-cr-biz-by-2028/ar-AA1od6ze?apiversion=v2&noservercache=1&domshim=1&renderwebcomponents=1&wcseo=1&batchservertelemetry=1&noservertelemetry=1 |access-date=2024-10-08 |website=www.msn.com}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=2017-08-18 |title=Kapil Sekhri's wine brotherhood |url=https://lifestyle.livemint.com//food/drink/kapil-sekhri-s-wine-brotherhood-111646830485428.html |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=Mintlounge |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":2">{{Cite news |last=Muthalaly |first=Shonali |date=2019-12-16 |title=Fratelli unveils its vintage 2019 wines |language=en-IN |work=The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/life-and-style/food/fratelli-unveils-its-vintage-2019-wines/article30320459.ece |access-date=2023-02-22 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref name=":3">{{Cite news |date=2022-12-13 |title=Tropical vineyards put India on the wine map |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/business-62993189 |access-date=2023-02-22}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2022-08-25 |title=Trade agreement: Why India made a U-turn on free trade deals |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-india-62559040 |access-date=2023-02-22}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2017-04-07 |title=Indian wines that have overcome the odds |work=Financial Times |url=https://www.ft.com/content/0e4e814a-1985-11e7-9c35-0dd2cb31823a |access-date=2023-02-24}}</ref><ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Fratelli Wines conferred with the Super: Best Family Business Led by a Woman |url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/companies/fratelli-wines-conferred-with-the-super-best-family-business-led-by-a-woman-8432141.html |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=Moneycontrol |language=en}}</ref>

== History ==
Fratelli means brothers in [[Italian language|Italian]] is a collaborative venture involving the Secci brothers from Italy and the Sekhri and Mohite-Patil brothers from India.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Sharma |first=Milan |date=2012-05-21 |title=How three families, Piero Masi come together to set up multicrore Indo-Italian wine venture Fratelli |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/small-biz/entrepreneurship/how-three-families-piero-masi-come-together-to-set-up-multicrore-indo-italian-wine-venture-fratelli/articleshow/13300413.cms?from=mdr |access-date=2024-01-09 |work=The Economic Times |issn=0013-0389}}</ref>

It was conceived in 2007<ref>{{Cite web |title=Fratelli Wines Private Limited Information - Fratelli Wines Private Limited Company Profile, Fratelli Wines Private Limited News on The Economic Times |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/company/ |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=The Economic Times |language=en |archive-date=2019-05-08 |archive-url=http://webarchive.loc.gov/all/20190508200151/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/company/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> by three sets of brothers: [[Italy|Italy's]] Secci brothers, Alessio and Andrea, [[New Delhi]]-based Sekhri brothers, Kapil and Gaurav, and Mohite-Patil Ranjit and Arjun from [[Solapur]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Muthalaly |first=Shonali |date=2020-12-02 |title=Fratelli's Sette: Raising a glass to a vintage year |language=en-IN |work=The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/life-and-style/food/raising-a-glass-to-a-vintage-year/article33230211.ece |access-date=2023-02-22 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Fratelli Wines director Kapil Sekhri dies |url=https://www.indiatoday.in/lifestyle/people/story/fratelli-wines-director-kapil-sekhri-dies-1730497-2020-10-11 |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=India Today |date=11 October 2020 |language=en}}</ref> Production is overseen by the [[Tuscany|Tuscan]] winemaker Piero Masi.<ref name=":4" />

The company has 240 acres of vineyard in [[Akluj]], [[Solapur]], [[Maharashtra]] and [[Karnataka]].<ref name=":4">{{Cite web |date=2017-01-10 |title=Home-grown brand Fratelli Wines to go global |url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/companies/home-grown-brand-fratelli-wines-to-go-global/article64099519.ece |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=www.thehindubusinessline.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Joshi |first=Hrishikesh |date=2010-07-22 |title=Fratelli Wines to launch four brands |work=Business Standard India |url=https://www.business-standard.com/article/companies/fratelli-wines-to-launch-four-brands-110072200017_1.html |access-date=2023-02-22}}</ref> The Vineyard is accessible to general public for staying and wine tasting.<ref name="india.com">{{Cite web |title=Travel Articles {{!}} Travel Blogs {{!}} Travel News & Information {{!}} Travel Guide {{!}} India.comFratelli Vineyards: the perfect weekend getaway for wine lovers! {{!}} India.com |url=https://www.india.com/travel/articles/fratelli-vineyards-the-perfect-weekend-getaway-for-wine-lovers-3231293/ |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=www.india.com |language=en}}</ref> Fratelli Wines are based on French grape varieties plus [[Sangiovese]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Fratelli Wines - Winery |url=https://www.wine-searcher.com/merchant/52801-fratelli-wines |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=Wine-Searcher |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Majumdar |first=Meghna |date=2019-09-30 |title=A taste of Fratelli's latest |language=en-IN |work=The Hindu |url=https://www.thehindu.com/life-and-style/food/fratelli-launhces-new-sette-wine/article29555414.ece |access-date=2023-02-22 |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref name=":2" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=2021-05-10 |title=9 Indian wines you should know about |url=https://www.architecturaldigest.in/story/9-indian-wines-you-should-know-about/ |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=Architectural Digest India |language=en-IN}}</ref>

In 2018, Fratelli started exporting wines to countries like [[France]] and the [[Netherlands]].<ref name=":1" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermes |date=2018-03-11 |title=Indian wine Fratelli going global {{!}} The Straits Times |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/lifestyle/food/indian-wine-going-global |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=www.straitstimes.com |language=en}}</ref>

== Brands ==
In 2015, Fratelli partnered with [[Jean-Charles Boisset]] to import some of its labels into India.<ref name=":0" /> In 2018, in partnership with [[Jean-Charles Boisset]], Fratelli launched its J'Noon brand of wines.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Junoon for Unique Wines brings J'noon from Fratelli & JCB |url=https://www.indianwineacademy.com/item_3_767.aspx |access-date=2023-03-10 |website=www.indianwineacademy.com}}</ref>

In 2020, Fratelli launched four flavours of wine in [[Drink can|cans]], to target young population.TiLT is a canned wine offering various flavors, including Red, White, Bubbly, and Bubbly Rosé. It has gained attention for its innovative approach to wine.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Vishal |first=Anoothi |date=2020-10-13 |title=Wine in a can, now in India |url=https://www.thehindu.com/life-and-style/food/raise-your-wine-in-a-can/article61718797.ece |access-date=2023-02-22 |work=The Hindu |language=en-IN |issn=0971-751X}}</ref><ref name=":3" />

In 2021, Fratelli Wines launched a line of [[cheese]] to accompany their wines.<ref>{{Cite web |last=IANS |date=2021-02-06 |title=Now Artisanal Cheese from the house of Fratelli Wines |url=https://www.thestatesman.com/lifestyle/now-artisanal-cheese-house-fratelli-wines-1502950640.html |access-date=2023-02-22 |website=The Statesman |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="india.com" />

